<title>USA: Amgen sells $100 mln in century bonds.</title>
<headline>Amgen sells $100 mln in century bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of</p>
<p>100-year bonds from Amgen Inc was priced on Thursday via</p>
<p>co-lead managers, Morgan Stanely &amp; Co Inc and Merrill Lynch &amp;</p>
<p>Co.</p>
<p>Amgen is a biopharmaceutical company based in Thousand</p>
<p>Oaks, California.</p>
<p>BORROWER AMGEN INC</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	 COUPON 8.125 PCT  MATURITY 4/1/2097</p>
<p>TYPE BONDS	   ISS PRICE 99.458  FIRST PAY DATE 10/1/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD 8.169 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-A  SPREAD 105 BPS    CALLABLE NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>NOTE: Make-whole call at Treasuries plus 20 basis points. ((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1662))</p>
</text>
